---
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Acaiaca Institute — Human Judgment in an AI-Augmented World"
  description="Acaiaca Institute studies what human judgment requires and what changes when increasingly capable artificial systems participate in human activity."
  canonicalPath="/"
>
  <Header />

  <main>
    <section class="hero page-shell" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <p class="eyebrow hero-eyebrow">Human judgment in an AI-augmented world</p>

      <h1 id="hero-title">
        We study what human judgment requires—and what changes when increasingly capable systems participate in it.
      </h1>

      <div class="hero-definition">
        <p>
          Acaiaca Institute exists to understand, preserve, and amplify human judgment in an AI-augmented world. Its research examines how judgment, agency, authority, participation, and responsibility are affected as artificial systems participate more deeply in human activity.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-bridge">
        <p>
          As AI systems increasingly remember, recommend, decide, and act, people face new questions about what should remain human, what can be shared or delegated, who possesses authority, and who remains responsible for what follows. Acaiaca investigates those questions rather than assuming their answers.
        </p>

        <div class="hero-actions" aria-label="Homepage pathways">
          <a class="cta-link" href="/research/">
            Explore the research <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
          <a class="secondary-link" href="/about/">
            What is Acaiaca? <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="hero-posture">
        Inquiry before doctrine. Evidence before certainty. Operationalization only where the work earns it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section
      class="principles page-shell"
      aria-labelledby="principles-title"
    >
      <header class="principles-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">Research principles &amp; normative commitments</p>

        <h2 id="principles-title">
          What constrains how we pursue the work.
        </h2>

        <div class="principles-distinction">
          <p>Acaiaca distinguishes between:</p>

          <dl>
            <div>
              <dt>Research Principles</dt>
              <dd>disciplines governing the integrity of inquiry</dd>
            </div>

            <div>
              <dt>Normative Commitments</dt>
              <dd>
                institutional constraints Acaiaca chooses to uphold while pursuing,
                interpreting, communicating, testing, and applying knowledge
              </dd>
            </div>
          </dl>

          <p class="principles-clarification">
            These are not research findings. They are declared constraints Acaiaca places upon itself.
          </p>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="principles-groups">
        <section
          class="principle-group"
          aria-labelledby="research-principles-title"
        >
          <header class="group-header">
            <p class="group-index" aria-hidden="true">01</p>

            <div>
              <h3 id="research-principles-title">Research Principles</h3>
              <p>Disciplines governing the integrity of inquiry.</p>
            </div>
          </header>

          <ol class="principle-list">
            <li>
              <span class="item-index" aria-hidden="true">01</span>

              <div>
                <h4>Inquiry can change our view</h4>
                <p>
                  Important claims should remain exposed to evidence, reasoning,
                  criticism, comparison, and counterexample capable of materially
                  changing them.
                </p>
              </div>
            </li>

            <li>
              <span class="item-index" aria-hidden="true">02</span>

              <div>
                <h4>Claims should not exceed their evidence</h4>
                <p>
                  Questions, propositions, observations, experiments, findings,
                  and institutional positions should be represented at the strength
                  their evidence supports.
                </p>
              </div>
            </li>

            <li>
              <span class="item-index" aria-hidden="true">03</span>

              <div>
                <h4>
                  Formal human presence does not by itself establish meaningful
                  human involvement
                </h4>
                <p>
                  A human approval step or nominal oversight is not, by itself,
                  evidence of meaningful understanding, participation, practical
                  control, authority, or responsibility.
                </p>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <section
          class="principle-group commitment-group"
          aria-labelledby="normative-commitments-title"
        >
          <header class="group-header">
            <p class="group-index" aria-hidden="true">02</p>

            <div>
              <h3 id="normative-commitments-title">Normative Commitments</h3>
              <p>
                Institutional constraints Acaiaca chooses to uphold while pursuing
                the work.
              </p>
            </div>
          </header>

          <ol class="principle-list">
            <li>
              <span class="item-index" aria-hidden="true">01</span>

              <div>
                <h4>Capability does not create legitimate authority</h4>
                <p>
                  Greater intelligence, accuracy, speed, expertise, or technical
                  capability does not by itself establish a right to decide or act.
                </p>
              </div>
            </li>

            <li>
              <span class="item-index" aria-hidden="true">02</span>

              <div>
                <h4>
                  Inquiry remains independent of commercial and institutional
                  convenience
                </h4>
                <p>
                  Acaiaca’s reputation, continuity, or potential commercial
                  interests should not determine research conclusions in advance.
                </p>
              </div>
            </li>

            <li>
              <span class="item-index" aria-hidden="true">03</span>

              <div>
                <h4>
                  Institutional representation should remain truthful and
                  proportionate
                </h4>
                <p>
                  Acaiaca should represent its evidence, maturity, contribution,
                  affiliations, participation opportunities, commercial readiness,
                  and authority without using institutional form or presentation as
                  a substitute for earned credibility.
                </p>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </section>
      </div>

      <div class="principles-link">
        <a class="cta-link" href="/research/principles/">
          View all research principles &amp; commitments
          <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="judgment page-shell" aria-labelledby="judgment-title">
      <header class="judgment-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">Foundational subject · Working Account</p>
        <h2 id="judgment-title">Judgment</h2>
        <p class="judgment-definition">
          Judgment is the capacity to reach a considered conclusion about what is
          true, appropriate, permissible, preferable, or to be done in a particular situation.
        </p>
        <div class="judgment-scope">
          <p>
            Acaiaca uses <strong>judgment</strong> as a broad institutional umbrella
            while using narrower established terminology when a narrower phenomenon
            is actually under examination.
          </p>
          <p>
            The current Working Account is offered especially as a candidate account
            of <strong>complex, multi-consideration judgment</strong> rather than as
            a settled model of every form of judgment.
          </p>
        </div>
      </header>

      <figure class="judgment-model" aria-describedby="judgment-boundary">
        <figcaption id="judgment-model-caption">
          A complex judgment may require an agent to:
        </figcaption>
        <aside class="judgment-context" aria-label="Context surrounding the model">
          <p>under uncertainty</p>
          <p>in anticipation of consequence</p>
        </aside>
        <ol class="judgment-elements" aria-labelledby="judgment-model-caption">
          <li>
            <div class="judgment-element">
              <h3>Situation / Reality</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="judgment-summary">encounter a situation</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="judgment-element">
              <h3>Relevant Considerations</h3>
              <p>What matters here?</p>
            </div>
            <p class="judgment-summary">recognize relevant considerations</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="judgment-element">
              <h3>Constraint Structure</h3>
              <p>What governs? Why? Within what scope?</p>
            </div>
            <p class="judgment-summary">
              form a constraint structure around what matters, what governs, and where it applies
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="judgment-element">
              <h3>Reconciliation</h3>
              <p>What can be satisfied together? What cannot?</p>
            </div>
            <p class="judgment-summary">reconcile compatible and conflicting considerations</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="judgment-element">
              <h3>Considered Conclusion</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="judgment-summary">reach a considered conclusion</p>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </figure>

      <div class="judgment-boundaries">
        <div id="judgment-boundary">
          <p class="judgment-boundary-lead">
            This is a synthetic account of what complex judgment may be accomplishing.
          </p>
          <p>
            It is <strong>not</strong> a claim that human cognition literally executes
            these stages in sequence. Nor does the model equate judgment with
            intent → action → consequence → learning. Those relationships belong
            to the broader human–AI agency problem.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="judgment-boundary-lead">
            What an agent treats as governing and what should legitimately govern
            are distinct questions.
          </p>
          <p>
            The Working Account helps expose the first without silently settling the second.
          </p>
          <a class="cta-link" href="/research/judgment/">
            Explore the Judgment Thesis <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="research-areas page-shell" aria-labelledby="research-areas-title">
      <header class="research-areas-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">Current Research Areas</p>
        <h2 id="research-areas-title">Where Acaiaca’s questions are beginning to cluster.</h2>
        <div class="research-areas-scope">
          <p>These are current clusters of inquiry, not fixed departments or settled programs.</p>
          <p>
            They may merge, divide, narrow, adopt established disciplinary names,
            remain informal, or disappear as the work develops. The Research Agenda
            currently treats them as emerging or candidate research programs whose
            status must be earned through accumulated inquiry.
          </p>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="research-landscape">
        <section class="research-area agency-area" aria-labelledby="agency-title">
          <h3 id="agency-title">Human–AI Agency</h3>
          <p class="research-question">
            How does artificial participation change people’s practical ability to
            understand, influence, redirect, challenge, revoke, or exit AI-mediated activity?
          </p>
          <a class="cta-link" href="/research/human-ai-agency/">
            Explore Human–AI Agency <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </section>

        <div class="research-area-pair">
          <section class="research-area" aria-labelledby="delegation-title">
            <h3 id="delegation-title">Delegation &amp; Authority</h3>
            <p class="research-question">
              What may legitimately be delegated, under what conditions, and how
              should authority be bounded, represented, subdelegated, revoked, or audited?
            </p>
            <a class="cta-link" href="/research/delegation-authority/">
              Explore Delegation &amp; Authority <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </a>
          </section>

          <section class="research-area" aria-labelledby="responsibility-title">
            <h3 id="responsibility-title">Responsibility in AI-Mediated Systems</h3>
            <p class="research-question">
              What happens when understanding, practical control, formal authority,
              execution, and consequence-bearing are distributed across different
              human and artificial actors?
            </p>
            <a class="cta-link" href="/research/responsibility/">
              Explore Responsibility <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </a>
          </section>
        </div>

        <section class="research-area sovereignty-area" aria-labelledby="sovereignty-title">
          <h3 id="sovereignty-title">Digital Sovereignty</h3>
          <p class="research-question">
            How can people and institutions retain meaningful authority and control
            over digital identity, information, memory, permissions, persistent
            context, and computational relationships that materially affect their agency?
          </p>
          <a class="cta-link" href="/research/digital-sovereignty/">
            Explore Digital Sovereignty <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </section>

        <section class="research-area society-area" aria-labelledby="society-title">
          <h3 id="society-title">Digital Civil Society</h3>
          <p class="research-question">
            How might participation, representation, legitimacy, governance, and
            collective judgment change when artificial systems become persistent
            participants or representatives in social coordination?
          </p>
          <a class="cta-link" href="/research/digital-civil-society/">
            Explore Digital Civil Society <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </section>
      </div>

      <div class="research-agenda-link">
        <a class="cta-link" href="/research/">
          Explore the Research Agenda <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="research-motion page-shell" aria-labelledby="research-motion-title">
      <header class="motion-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">Research in Motion</p>
        <p class="motion-selection">
          Selected propositions, working frameworks, and provisional constructs
        </p>
        <h2 id="research-motion-title">
          The work develops at different speeds and in different forms.
        </h2>
      </header>

      <div class="motion-objects">
        <article class="motion-object" aria-labelledby="assistance-title">
          <header class="motion-identity">
            <h3 id="assistance-title">AI Assistance, Judgment &amp; Practical Agency</h3>
            <p class="motion-metadata">Proposition · Proposed</p>
          </header>
          <p class="motion-question">
            Under what conditions can artificial assistance improve human judgment
            performance without materially reducing practical agency?
          </p>
          <div class="motion-notes">
            <p>This corresponds to Research Agenda proposition P8, currently Proposed.</p>
            <p>
              The Intellectual Landscape characterizes this as a genuinely open and
              high-value question: performance improvement has substantial adjacent
              evidence, while preservation of practical agency remains less
              standardized and may require longitudinal study.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="motion-object motion-construct" aria-labelledby="persistent-state-title">
          <header class="motion-identity">
            <h3 id="persistent-state-title">Persistent Agentic State</h3>
            <p class="motion-metadata">Provisional construct · Digital Sovereignty</p>
          </header>
          <p class="motion-question">
            Does treating identity, authorization, memory and context, preferences
            and policies, adaptive state, provenance, and relational state together
            reveal governance problems that are missed when those layers are treated separately?
          </p>
          <div class="motion-notes">
            <p>
              Persistent Agentic State remains a provisional layered umbrella within
              Digital Sovereignty rather than an independent research program merely
              because it is important.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="motion-object" aria-labelledby="constraint-architecture-title">
          <header class="motion-identity">
            <h3 id="constraint-architecture-title">Constraint Architecture</h3>
            <p class="motion-metadata">Working framework · Comparative evaluation</p>
          </header>
          <p class="motion-question">
            Can heterogeneous considerations relevant to complex judgment be represented
            explicitly without collapsing important distinctions or introducing excessive
            rigidity, cognitive burden, or false precision?
          </p>
          <div class="motion-notes">
            <p>
              Constraint Architecture remains a provisional representational synthesis
              under comparative evaluation rather than a claimed novel general decision method.
            </p>
            <p>
              Its continued value depends on whether it complements or improves upon
              strong established approaches without creating false precision or unnecessary rigidity.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="motion-link">
        <a class="cta-link" href="/research/">
          View current research <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="how-works page-shell" aria-labelledby="how-works-title">
      <header class="works-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">How Acaiaca Works</p>
        <h2 id="how-works-title">Explain. Test. Operationalize.</h2>
        <div class="works-framing">
          <p>
            These are principal institutional operating functions.
            They are <strong>not a mandatory pipeline</strong>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Ideas may originate in research, public discussion, outside scholarship,
            observation, practical experience, experimentation, implementation,
            criticism, or other legitimate sources and move among functions repeatedly.
          </p>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="works-functions">
        <section class="works-explain" aria-labelledby="explain-title">
          <h3 id="explain-title"><span aria-hidden="true">01</span> Explain</h3>
          <h4>Humanity Is the Loop</h4>
          <p class="works-metadata">Active public communication project</p>
          <p>
            Humanity Is the Loop makes Acaiaca’s questions, research, experiments,
            distinctions, and institutional thinking understandable enough to engage,
            challenge, and use.
          </p>
          <p>
            Its purpose is not to make Acaiaca appear correct.
            Its purpose is to make inquiry legible.
          </p>
          <p class="works-emphasis works-home">
            Acaiaca Institute is the institutional home. Humanity Is the Loop is the public voice.
          </p>
          <a class="cta-link" href="/projects/humanity-is-the-loop/">
            Explore Humanity Is the Loop <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </section>

        <section class="works-test" aria-labelledby="test-title">
          <h3 id="test-title"><span aria-hidden="true">02</span> Test</h3>
          <h4>Acaiaca Labs</h4>
          <p class="works-metadata">Testing and experimentation function</p>
          <p>
            Acaiaca Labs brings questions, premises, propositions, models, and
            prototypes into contact with evidence and conditions capable of changing Acaiaca’s view.
          </p>
          <div class="works-methods">
            <p>Testing may include:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>literature comparison;</li>
              <li>conceptual analysis;</li>
              <li>experiments;</li>
              <li>prototypes;</li>
              <li>simulations;</li>
              <li>bounded research environments;</li>
              <li>evaluation frameworks;</li>
              <li>experimental software;</li>
              <li>field inquiry;</li>
              <li>structured observation;</li>
              <li>replication;</li>
              <li>case analysis.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <p class="works-emphasis">Labs may build to learn.</p>
          <p>A prototype does not become a product merely because it works.</p>
          <a class="cta-link" href="/labs/">
            Explore Acaiaca Labs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </section>

        <section class="works-systems" aria-labelledby="operationalize-title">
          <h3 id="operationalize-title"><span aria-hidden="true">03</span> Operationalize</h3>
          <h4>Acaiaca Systems</h4>
          <p class="works-metadata">Anticipated</p>
          <p>
            Acaiaca Systems is the reserved institutional home for work that may
            eventually warrant durable operational implementation as systems,
            software, products, or services.
          </p>
          <p class="works-emphasis">
            Systems may build to operate.<br />
            Systems follows evidence and implementation.
          </p>
          <p>
            Operationalization is one possible outcome.
            It is not the required destination of successful inquiry.
          </p>
          <a class="cta-link" href="/systems/">
            About Acaiaca Systems <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="research-evolves page-shell" aria-labelledby="research-evolves-title">
      <header class="evolves-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">How the Research Evolves</p>
        <h2 id="research-evolves-title">Acaiaca expects to change its mind.</h2>
      </header>

      <div class="inquiry-diagram">
        <ol class="inquiry-loop" aria-label="Recursive inquiry sequence">
          <li>
            <span class="inquiry-label" id="research-inquiry" tabindex="-1">Inquiry</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="inquiry-fork">
              <span class="inquiry-label">Explain / Test</span>
              <aside class="inquiry-optional" aria-labelledby="optional-operationalize-title">
                <p class="inquiry-condition">Optional branch</p>
                <h3 id="optional-operationalize-title">Operationalize</h3>
                <p>From sufficiently mature work, where warranted.</p>
              </aside>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li><span class="inquiry-label">Evidence &amp; Observation</span></li>
          <li><span class="inquiry-label">Compare</span></li>
          <li><span class="inquiry-label">Revise</span></li>
          <li>
            <span class="inquiry-label">Renewed Inquiry <span aria-hidden="true">↺</span></span>
            <a class="inquiry-return" href="#research-inquiry">Return to Inquiry</a>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div class="evolves-principle">
        <p>
          No premise or proposition is entitled to survive because effort has
          already been invested in it. No prototype is entitled to become a product because it works.
        </p>
        <a class="cta-link" href="/research/methods/">
          Methods, evidence &amp; revisions <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(12, minmax(0, 1fr));
    column-gap: clamp(1rem, 2.2vw, 2rem);
    row-gap: 0;
    padding-block: clamp(4.5rem, 9vw, 8.5rem) clamp(5rem, 9vw, 8rem);
  }

  .hero-eyebrow {
    grid-column: 1 / span 3;
    align-self: start;
    padding-top: 0.65rem;
  }

  h1 {
    grid-column: 4 / -1;
    max-width: 11.25em;
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--step-4);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.038em;
    line-height: 0.99;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .hero-definition,
  .hero-bridge {
    margin-top: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem);
    border-top: var(--rule);
    padding-top: 1.35rem;
  }

  .hero-definition {
    grid-column: 4 / span 4;
  }

  .hero-bridge {
    grid-column: 9 / -1;
  }

  .hero-definition p,
  .hero-bridge p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: clamp(0.98rem, 0.92rem + 0.16vw, 1.08rem);
    line-height: 1.72;
  }

  .hero-definition p {
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
  }

  .hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.65rem 1.6rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .cta-link span,
  .secondary-link span {
    margin-left: 0.28rem;
  }

  .secondary-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    min-height: 2.75rem;
    align-items: center;
    padding-block: 0.45rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    font-weight: 550;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .secondary-link:hover {
    color: var(--color-plum);
  }

  .hero-posture {
    grid-column: 4 / -1;
    margin: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem) 0 0;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-bronze);
    padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 1.2rem;
    color: var(--color-green);
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 0.96rem + 0.25vw, 1.24rem);
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .principles {
    border-top: var(--rule);
    padding-block: clamp(5.5rem, 10vw, 9rem);
  }

  .principles-intro {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(12, minmax(0, 1fr));
    column-gap: clamp(1rem, 2.2vw, 2rem);
  }

  .principles-intro > .eyebrow {
    grid-column: 1 / span 3;
    align-self: start;
    padding-top: 0.55rem;
  }

  .principles-intro h2 {
    grid-column: 4 / span 6;
    max-width: 8.5em;
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 1.9rem + 2.5vw, 4.8rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    line-height: 1.02;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .principles-distinction {
    grid-column: 9 / -1;
    padding-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .principles-distinction > p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .principles-distinction dl {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin: 1.15rem 0 1.3rem;
  }

  .principles-distinction dl div {
    border-top: var(--rule);
    padding-top: 0.85rem;
  }

  .principles-distinction dt {
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .principles-distinction dd {
    margin: 0.3rem 0 0;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .principles-clarification {
    color: var(--color-charcoal) !important;
